#doc (Manual) "Functional support and functional decompositions" =>

This chapter formalizes Sakai's Definitions 1.14.1--1.14.2 and Theorems
1.14.3--1.14.4.  For a normal positive functional $`\varphi` on a
$`W^*`-algebra, its GNS null space is a closed left ideal generated by a
projection.  The complement of that generator is the support of $`\varphi`.
Orthogonality of positive functionals is defined by Sakai's norm equality;
self-adjoint normal functionals have unique orthogonal positive/negative
decompositions; and arbitrary normal functionals have unique polar
decompositions with the source's right-multiplication convention.

The public progression is

$`
  \text{normal positive functional}
  \longrightarrow \text{null left ideal}
  \longrightarrow \text{support}
  \longrightarrow \text{greatest zero projection}
  \longrightarrow \text{support cutdown}
  \longrightarrow \text{faithful support corner}
  \longrightarrow \text{norm orthogonality}
  \longrightarrow \text{unique Jordan decomposition}
  \longrightarrow \text{unique general polar decomposition}.
`

The construction reuses the established projection-normality predicate,
closed-left-ideal classifier, projection order, and corner API.  It introduces
neither a second kind of normal functional nor a second notion of corner.

